T by NWS Denver CO","description":"* WHAT...Small stream flooding caused by excessive rainfall is\nexpected.\n\n* WHERE...Central Douglas County in northeastern Colorado...\n\n* WHEN...Until 430 PM MDT.\n\n* IMPACTS...Minor flooding in low-lying and poor drainage areas.\nRises in small streams and normally dry creeks.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n\n- At 129 PM MDT, Doppler radar and automated rain gauges\nindicated heavy rain due to thunderstorms. This may cause small\nstream flooding. Between 0.5 and 1 inch of rain has fallen.\n\n- This includes the following streams and drainages...\nEast Plum Creek, Plum Creek and Cherry Creek. Additional rainfall\namounts up to 1 inch are expected over the area. This additional\nrain will result in minor flooding.\n\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nCastle Rock.","ends":"2026-08-14T16:30:00-06:00","severity":"Minor","areaDesc":"Douglas, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.cc50b16a83b8fb9b862f67cf324ddddaea7290c3.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.cc50b16a83b8fb9b862f67cf324ddddaea7290c3.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"BOU","issued":"2026-08-14T19:11:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KBOU 141911 AFDBOU Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Denver/Boulder CO 111 PM MDT Fri Aug 14 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Flash flooding and a few severe storms will be the main threats through this evening, as another round of storms moves east- northeast across the forecast area. - Monsoon moisture lasts through the weekend, bringing scattered showers and thunderstorms each","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=BOU&issuedby=BOU&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":null,"fwf":{"office":"BOU","issued":"2026-08-14T19:23:00+00:00","snippet":".DISCUSSION...Rest of today through Saturday... Monsoonal moisture will remain high across the area through Saturday, with scattered to numerous showers and storms with wetting rainfall. Heavy rainfall rates may lead to localized flash flooding, par